== Case text (Ask-CK ck.db zephyr_cases, read-only)
Case:          AWPTCM-T18571  (Approved)
Title:         802.1Q Trunk a Dynamic Aggreagator
Objective:     To confirm that the dynamic aggreagator will work as normally as a trunked port
Precondition:  change the configuration such that the trunked port
Step 1 text (verbatim):     The 802.1Q trunked port should work equally as well being a dynamic Aggregator. Multiple source mac addresses should be sent from the Ixia
Step 1 test data:           (empty)
Step 1 expected (verbatim): There should be no 4 byte deficit per frame in traffic flow

== Method
As T18570 (18570/work/run1.log), with an LACP (dynamic) aggregator in place of the static one: x230 port1.0.2 + port1.0.3
`channel-group 12 mode active` -> po12, an 802.1Q trunk with VLAN 106 tagged (native VLAN 1); the stack's port1.0.2 (out of
static sa2) + port1.0.17 `channel-group 12 mode active` -> po12, same trunk. eth3 -> x230 port1.0.5 (access 106) -> po12 ->
stack po12 -> port3.0.13 (access 106) -> eth1. No Ixia: tools/linerate.py with 64 rotating source MACs per sender, line
rate both ways, maximum standard frames (1518 untagged / 1522 tagged on the trunk) plus 1500-byte frames, every receive
counter with --rx-len (only frames of exactly the sent length count). Unlearned destination MACs (flood within VLAN 106
only), TTL 1.

